egyptian mummies chinese mummies the  scorpion king ever wonder how all these  undead characters fit together and what  about the adventurers trying to find  them keep watching for an explanation of  the entire timeline of the mummy  franchise  the story of the mummy franchise begins  over 5000 years before rick o'connell  battled the titular egyptian priest  imhotep in the 1920s  around the year 3087 bc a boy named  matthias is an acadian child who's  destined to become the man known all  over the ancient world as the scorpion  king he's also a 13 year old with  ambitions of becoming a black scorpion  this elite unit served the kingdom of  akkad and protected its leader from harm  though it was far from a glamorous life  when the trainer of the scorpions the  battle heart and sargon discovered that  matthias's female friend layla had snuck  into the training sessions in disguise  he wasn't happy he told the girl that  there were no female scorpions and  expelled her which angered mathias the  youngster lashed out at sargon and asher  was forced to defend his son from him  king hamurabi stepped in to stop the  scuffle before someone got hurt but the  chassen sagon swore revenge on asher  using his dark magic sargon killed  matthias's dad in a cowardly attack  seven years after the murder of his  father a 20-year-old matthias finished  his training and became a fully fledged  black scorpion the ruler of akkad had  been killed and usurped by sargon who  then used the cursed arrow to kill  matthias's younger brother noah  [Applause]  the now grown-up layla confirmed to  matthias that sargon was using dark  magic and that they would need a special  weapon to defeat him leaving a cod  behind mathias journeyed to the  underworld to retrieve the sword of  damocles after burning off his black  scorpion tattoo with it he used the  legendary weapon to take revenge on the  man that killed his father and brother  akkad quickly fell into ruin after the  reign of the evil usurper sargon by 3077  bc there were only three akkadians left  matthias his half brother jessop and  their friend rama they earned a living  as mercenaries in the years following  the collapse of akkad gaining a fearsome  reputation  they were not quite as feared as the  great swordsman and warlord memnon  however memnon had cut a bloody path  across the known world using the  predictions of a sorcerer named  cassandra to stay one step ahead of his  enemies in a last-ditch effort to stop  him king pharaoh of the free tribes  hired the last accordions to kill the  sorcerer the akkadian successfully  located cassandra but jessup and rama  were killed by mimnon's men who were  tipped off by king pharaon's turncoat  son matthias managed to escape with his  life and the sorcerer who it turned out  was an unwilling accomplice to mimnon's  conquest she used her magic to save  matthias from an arrow dipped in  scorpion venom but it changed him  forever  the blood of the scorpion will always  flow through his veins  she predicted that he would likely die  if he faced mimnon though matthias beat  the odds defeating the warlord and  becoming the new ruler of gomorrah the  city's troops dubbed him the scorpion  king  matthias married cassandra after they  took down memnon and they enjoyed a  period of peace and prosperity but it  would not last nothing lasts forever my  king  when we next caught up with matthias in  2012's the scorpion king 3 battle for  redemption we learned that cassandra was  among the many who perished from a  deadly plague that brought his kingdom  to its knees mathias returned to his  life as a mercenary and found himself in  the employee of another ruler king aorus  of egypt had a job for matthias to stop  his upstart younger brother talis who is  planning to usurp him with magic mathias  traveled to the far east to face talus  and defeated him despite talus using the  black book to raise warriors from the  dead in an attempt to give him the upper  hand  years after taking out talus mathias got  a new job from a new king he was sent to  find and acquire an artifact known as  the urn of kings which he did but not  without a fight during the scuffle his  apprentice drozen proved himself to be a  traitor who was after the urn it's  revealed later that inside the urn is  the golden key of lord alchemin and it  leads to alchemin's crown which gives  the wearer unimaginable power drazen  killed his own father and tried to frame  matthias all in an attempt to get the  crown for himself but it's all to no  avail mathias found out the location of  the crown 2 and witnesses drazen meet  his own demise after seeing its power  first hand he reported back that it was  just a myth and locked it away again for  the good of humanity turns out it was  just a campfire story  the last adventure the scorpion king  would go on before his ill-fated assault  on thebes was when matthias teamed up  with a female warrior named tala in 2018  scorpion king book of souls the film  pits matthias against tala's brother  nebzarik who has raided the tomb of the  ancient king memtep to acquire the fang  of anubis nebzarek planned on using it  to rule the world but that wasn't the  only thing on his to-do list he also  wanted the scorpion king dead the only  way to neutralize the fang of anubis was  to use it to stab the book of souls but  that became more complicated when  matthias learned that the book was not  actually a book but a person memtep's  daughter was the living embodiment of  the book and she ultimately sacrificed  herself to break the curse and free the  trapped souls  after years of trying to avoid violence  losing so many friends and loved ones  took its toll on matthias by the year  3067 bc he had resumed the title of  scorpion king and assembled a massive  army intent on taking over the known  world and imposing his rule as seen in  the prologue to the mummy returns he led  an assault on the great city of thebes  but failed to take the city after a  brutal bloody campaign that lasted for  seven years he and his army were  defeated and driven into the sacred  desert of amshir under the blistering  sun his men began dropping like flies  until only matthias himself remained  alone angry and desperate he called on  anubis and made him an offer grant the  power to defeat his enemies once and for  all and he could have his soul anubis  accepted an oasis sprang up around  matthias saving his life anubis gave him  command of his army and he made easy  work of those who defied him taking  thebes with little effort as soon as the  city fell however anubis collected the  debt the scorpion king was taken to the  underworld now bound to serve the dark  god  many years later in 1290 bc to be exact  pharaoh seti the first high priest  imhotep entered into a secret affair  with his lord's concubine enoch soon the  moon she spent her days painted with an  intricate gold pattern one that easily  smudged if anyone touched her seti would  know when he noticed that she had been  touched and began to grill her about it  imhotep acted he and anak sunamun  stabbed the pharaoh to death as his  daughter watched on from an adjacent  balcony she alerted her father's guards  and rather than be captured hanaksu  namoon committed suicide imhotep was  spirited away by his followers and made  it his mission to resurrect his lover he  stole the book of the dead but the magi  stopped him before he could complete the  ritual he was sentenced to the most  brutal punishment of the day the ham  died the victim's tongue was cut out and  they were mummified alive with a bunch  of flesh-eating scarab beetles thrown  into the sarcophagus for good measure  in the year 200 bc emperor han of  ancient china set in motion the events  that would play out on screen in the  mummy tomb of the dragon emperor han  wanted to live forever so he sought the  help of the powerful sorcerer c-u-n the  sorcerer was sent on a mission to  retrieve some magic 